      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.04486",
      "dcterms:abstract": "In this chapter, we review the Ra˜nada ﬁeld line solutions of Maxwell’s equations in the vacuum, which describe a topologically non-trivial electro- magnetic ﬁeld, as well as their relation with the knot theory. Also, we present a generalization of these solutions to the non-linear electrodynamics recently published in the literature.",
